module lib/hf/mdg_eri
  The production electron repulsion integrals and direct J and K, on the
  kernels lib/cas generated (lib/hf/mdg_kernels). The method is lib/hf/md_eri's:
  a store of shell pairs prepared once, then each shell quartet as two
  matrix products over the pairs' E matrices and one R table per primitive
  quartet. The R tables and the pair expansions come from the generated
  defs, a spherical basis gets spherical rows in the store so no quartet is
  transformed, and the E matrices are kept instead of copied for each
  quartet. md_eri and md_direct stay as the general code that checks it.

mdg_t2  @2543cdfa
  why   The store moves each pair's E rows to spherical functions once, so this is the one transform a spherical quartet needs, built per pair from the block-diagonal `M`.
  M       the Cartesian-to-spherical matrix of lib/hf/cart2sph, `[nao_cart, nao_sph]`; read only when `sph = 1`
  shells  the shells table
  sa      the first group's first shell (or the bra shell)
  sb      the second group's first shell (or the ket shell)
  na      the first shell's Cartesian components
  nb      the second shell's Cartesian components
  ma      the first shell's spherical components
  mb      the second shell's spherical components
  T       the pair transform `(M_a (x) M_b)^T`

